Updated `src/blog/people/drafts/David-Beckham.md`.

## Main changes

**Sandra Beckham now exists in the profile.** The origin section carried the whole thesis on one parent. I added her, plus Ted's own on-camera justification from the Netflix series: *"No. If I told him how good he was, then he's got nothing to work at."* That's the draft's argument stated by the man who built the engine, which beats the "too strict" paraphrase the review proposed. Section now closes on the 2002 separation after 33 years.

**Added the football.** The 17 August 1996 halfway-line goal against Wimbledon (Selhurst Park, Neil Sullivan off his line, "It changed my life"), plus the dead-ball repetition in the diagnosis section. A piece arguing the gift was manufactured now shows the manufactured thing.

**Qatar is now specifically his contradiction.** It opens with the June 2002 *Attitude* cover, the first Premier League footballer on a gay magazine, and his verbatim line. Lycett's stunt now names the prop: he shredded that same cover. Left unresolved, as the review recommended.

**Inter Miami is shown, not asserted.** The $25m expansion clause in the 2007 Galaxy contract, the collapsed stadium sites, the November 2018 Melreese referendum, 2020 debut, Messi 2023. Sixteen years on a timeline he couldn't compress, which also sets up the ending.

**Ending swapped.** "Repair between adults requires another person's consent" moved from mid-piece to the close; the closer no longer re-narrates the flat-pack hive, 4am and "peace," and lands on the cost instead of resolving into peace. Also rewrote the inner-thought block to carry the fear under the ritual rather than repeat the cold open.

Also closed the charity gap the knighthood citation opens, and trimmed the duplicate reserve-counterevidence, two soft disclaimers, and timeline entries restating prose told in full elsewhere.

## Two things worth your attention

**I edited a script, not just the draft.** The Neville pull-quote graded VAGUE only because `Stick to Football` was missing from `blog-source-audit.mjs`'s OUTLETS list, while `Joe Rogan Experience` and `Club Shay Shay` are already there. I added it with a dated comment matching the file's convention. That's outside the command's usual scope, so flagging it explicitly.

**I rejected two of the review's facts.** The "very honoured to have the tag of gay icon" quote circulates widely but I could not trace it to a primary source, so I used the verifiable *Attitude* line instead. And I did not use Ted's memoir as the cause of the 2002 separation, unverified, and asserting a cause there would be the exact private-motive claim the profile refuses everywhere else. The date is stated; the cause is not.

